IED.\n\n## BOTTOM LINE\nParallelism is **mostly the wrong lever** for the stated goal. The \"don't parallelize code-writing\" rule is correct; the boundary is sharper than the one-line rule states. Two independent reasons make write-parallelism lose (it is \"over-determined\"):\n\n1. **Conflict-safety.** Parallel writers conflict on **semantic interface con","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false}}
