{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01PzeqsWQT3Atrop8vz64Xvc","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# Gandalf runtime — the RAW-DRAFT contract (Tier-1)\n2\t\n3\t> What the model emits in runtime mode, and what the host does with it. The model emits **only** the\n4\t> raw draft below as its final message — it does **NOT** self-assign tiers or refutation stamps. The\n5\t> host (`runtime/gandalf-run.mjs` → `runtime/seam-pass.applySeamPass`) applies the shipped seams and\n6\t> produces the canary-conformant, honestly-graded `schema/advisor-output.schema.json` output.\n7\t\n8\t## Why a contract (journal/0001 + LESSONS.md)\n9\t\n10\tThe first real Gandalf runs showed the model produces excellent DIAGNOSE / SITUATE / ANTICIPATE\n11\t**content** but, asked to also stamp the honest tiers itself, keeps hand-approximating them and failing\n12\tthe B-honesty canary. The honest tiers + stamps are the **seam's** job, applied deterministically. So\n13\tthe model's job is reduced to emitting the raw findings; the host stamps them. **Do not narrate a tier\n14\tor a \"no independent refutation ran\" stamp in `reasoning` — emit the raw fields and let the host apply\n15\tthe seam.**\n16\t\n17\t## Emit ONLY this JSON object (the raw draft)\n18\t\n19\t```jsonc\n20\t{\n21\t  \"reasoning\": \"<the deep-think reasoning — emitted BEFORE the verdict>\",\n22\t  \"verdict\":   \"<the overall verdict; may be 'this is sound'>\",\n23\t\n24\t  \"findings\":  [ /* diagnose / situate / anticipate findings — see per-kind shape below */ ],\n25\t  \"nitpicks\":  [ /* minor, low-stakes findings: { id, rung, reasoning, verdict } */ ],\n26\t  \"elevations\":[ /* forward, value-adding suggestions — see shape below; NO tier, NO stamp */ ]\n27\t}\n28\t```\n29\t\n30\t`reasoning`, `verdict` are required non-empty strings; `findings`, `nitpicks`, `elevations` are\n31\trequired arrays (may be empty). A malformed draft (missing a required key, a non-object item, an\n32\tanticipate finding missing its future-state) is **rejected** by the host with a non-zero exit and an\n33\thonest stderr message — **no partial / forged output is written.**\n34\t\n35\t### `findings[]` — per `kind` (the fields each seam consumes)\n36\t\n37\t**`kind: \"diagnose\"`** — a vetted-core diagnosis. Do NOT add `gandalf_core`; the host stamps it\n38\t(`stampDiagnoseCoreProvenance`). Do NOT carry any external commission id (diagnosis is the core's).\n39\t```jsonc\n40\t{ \"id\": \"d-1\", \"kind\": \"diagnose\", \"rung\": \"<REFUTED|UNVERIFIED|CLAIMED|CORROBORATED|OBSERVED>\",\n41\t  \"reasoning\": \"...\", \"verdict\": \"...\", \"severity\": \"<minor|major|critical>\"? }\n42\t```\n43\t\n44\t**`kind: \"anticipate\"`** — a bounded, forward-looking premortem on the SINGLE effort. Emit the two\n45\tfuture-state fields; the host composes the finding (`composeAnticipation` sets `subject_cardinality: 1`\n46\tand refuses any regret / counterfactual-cost field).\n47\t```jsonc\n48\t{ \"id\": \"a-1\", \"kind\": \"anticipate\", \"rung\": \"UNVERIFIED\",\n49\t  \"reasoning\": \"...\", \"verdict\": \"...\",\n50\t  \"future_state_condition\": \"<a not-yet-present condition>\",\n51\t  \"enabling_assumption\":    \"<what must hold for it to arrive>\",\n52\t  \"severity\": \"<minor|major|critical>\"? }\n53\t```\n54\t\n55\t**`kind: \"situate\"`** — a best-in-class framing. Emit the SITUATE pipeline stages; the host composes +\n56\thonesty-caps the finding (`composeSituate`). **Tier-1 has no live researchPrime commission**, so\n57\t`facts_verified` is `false` by construction and the host attaches the `needs_verification` handoff.\n58\t```jsonc\n59\t{ \"id\": \"s-1\", \"kind\": \"situate\", \"reasoning\": \"...\", \"verdict\": \"...\",\n60\t  \"abstraction\":  { \"stage\": \"S0-abstract\", \"skeleton\": \"<domain-neutral pattern>\" },\n61\t  \"commission\":   { \"skill\": \"researchPrime\", \"question\": \"...\", \"cross_model\": false,\n62\t                    \"origin_family\": \"fable-5\", \"independent_origin\": false,\n63\t                    \"researchprime_commission_id\": null },\n64\t  \"structure_map\": { \"answer\": \"<answer-first conclusion>\",\n65\t                     \"correspondences\": [\n66\t                       { \"source_relation\": \"...\", \"target_relation\": \"...\" },\n67\t                       { \"source_relation\": \"...\", \"target_relation\": \"...\" }  /* >= 2, RELATIONAL */\n68\t                     ] },\n69\t  \"outside_view_base_rate\": \"<the outside-view base rate>\" }\n70\t```\n71\t\n72\tA finding of any other `kind` (or none) passes through untouched. A finding with `rung: \"REFUTED\"`\n73\t**drops** (the only drop condition).\n74\t\n75\t### `elevations[]` — forward suggestions (NO tier, NO stamp)\n76\t\n77\tEmit the suggestion + the **named concrete defeater** (`what_would_refute_it`), never a tier or a\n78\tstamp. In Tier-1 no independent refuter runs, so the host downgrades **every** elevation to\n79\t`SPECULATIVE` and stamps it `\"no independent refutation ran\"` (`vetElevationRefutation` + `labelTier`).\n80\t```jsonc\n81\t{ \"id\": \"e-1\", \"value_if_true\": \"<low|medium|high>\", \"rung\": \"<...>\",\n82\t  \"reasoning\": \"...\", \"verdict\": \"...\",\n83\t  \"what_would_refute_it\": \"<a NAMED concrete defeater — never a confidence word>\",\n84\t  \"severity\": \"<minor|major|critical>\"? }\n85\t```\n86\tA `rung: \"REFUTED\"` elevation **drops**.\n87\t\n88\t## What the host applies (deterministically, never the model)\n89\t\n90\t| Stage | Seam | Effect |\n91\t|-------|------|--------|\n92\t| diagnose | `seam/diagnose-core.stampDiagnoseCoreProvenance` | appends `gandalf_core: { protocol: \"PROTOCOL v2\" }` |\n93\t| anticipate | `seam/anticipate.composeAnticipation` | `subject_cardinality: 1`; B3 + B9 enforced |\n94\t| situate | `seam/situate.composeSituate` | rung cap (no self-CORROBORATED) + `needs_verification` handoff |\n95\t| elevation | `seam/refute.vetElevationRefutation` → `seam/score-label.labelTier` | SPECULATIVE floor + stamp; single-family PROMISING ceiling |\n96\t| drop | `seam/score-label.dropsFromOutput` | only `rung: \"REFUTED\"` drops |\n97\t| synthesis | `seam/score-label.composeRiskLabels` | one `risk_labels` entry per present leg, envelope rung, PROMISING ceiling |\n98\t| degradation | (host roll-up) | any per-item `degraded: true` ⇒ top-level `degraded: true` (B6) |\n99\t\n100\tThe result is validated by the shipped `test/harness.assertIncrement1Conformant` before it is written;\n101\tif it would not pass, the host exits non-zero and writes nothing.\n102\t\n103\t## Scope note (Tier-1)\n104\t\n105\tThis host runs the **deterministic** seam pass on ONE model run. It does **not** dispatch the live\n106\tindependent named-defeater refuters or the researchPrime SITUATE commission (those need the `agent()`\n107\tseam the repo flags as the integration point the gate never runs). The **live-refuter PROMISING tier**\n108\tis the sequenced follow-on — see `LESSONS.md` and `journal/`.\n109\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"362da09a-6bbc-452b-8ae5-c2595173c969","uuid":"b784e76f-2156-4eb0-a904-3a01cd280c04","timestamp":"2026-06-23T18:46:07.695Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"C:\\dev\\Skill Foundry\\skills\\gandalf\\runtime\\RAW-DRAFT-CONTRACT.md","content":"# Gandalf runtime — the RAW-DRAFT contract (Tier-1)\n\n> What the model emits in runtime mode, and what the host does with it. The model emits **only** the\n> raw draft below as its final message — it does **NOT** self-assign tiers or refutation stamps. The\n> host (`runtime/gandalf-run.mjs` → `runtime/seam-pass.applySeamPass`) applies the shipped seams and\n> produces the canary-conformant, honestly-graded `schema/advisor-output.schema.json` output.\n\n## Why a contract (journal/0001 + LESSONS.md)\n\nThe first real Gandalf runs showed the model produces excellent DIAGNOSE / SITUATE / ANTICIPATE\n**content** but, asked to also stamp the honest tiers itself, keeps hand-approximating them and failing\nthe B-honesty canary. The honest tiers + stamps are the **seam's** job, applied deterministically. So\nthe model's job is reduced to emitting the raw findings; the host stamps them. **Do not narrate a tier\nor a \"no independent refutation ran\" stamp in `reasoning` — emit the raw fields and let the host apply\nthe seam.**\n\n## Emit ONLY this JSON object (the raw draft)\n\n```jsonc\n{\n  \"reasoning\": \"<the deep-think reasoning — emitted BEFORE the verdict>\",\n  \"verdict\":   \"<the overall verdict; may be 'this is sound'>\",\n\n  \"findings\":  [ /* diagnose / situate / anticipate findings — see per-kind shape below */ ],\n  \"nitpicks\":  [ /* minor, low-stakes findings: { id, rung, reasoning, verdict } */ ],\n  \"elevations\":[ /* forward, value-adding suggestions — see shape below; NO tier, NO stamp */ ]\n}\n```\n\n`reasoning`, `verdict` are required non-empty strings; `findings`, `nitpicks`, `elevations` are\nrequired arrays (may be empty). A malformed draft (missing a required key, a non-object item, an\nanticipate finding missing its future-state) is **rejected** by the host with a non-zero exit and an\nhonest stderr message — **no partial / forged output is written.**\n\n### `findings[]` — per `kind` (the fields each seam consumes)\n\n**`kind: \"diagnose\"`** — a vetted-core diagnosis. Do NOT add `gandalf_core`; the host stamps it\n(`stampDiagnoseCoreProvenance`). Do NOT carry any external commission id (diagnosis is the core's).\n```jsonc\n{ \"id\": \"d-1\", \"kind\": \"diagnose\", \"rung\": \"<REFUTED|UNVERIFIED|CLAIMED|CORROBORATED|OBSERVED>\",\n  \"reasoning\": \"...\", \"verdict\": \"...\", \"severity\": \"<minor|major|critical>\"? }\n```\n\n**`kind: \"anticipate\"`** — a bounded, forward-looking premortem on the SINGLE effort. Emit the two\nfuture-state fields; the host composes the finding (`composeAnticipation` sets `subject_cardinality: 1`\nand refuses any regret / counterfactual-cost field).\n```jsonc\n{ \"id\": \"a-1\", \"kind\": \"anticipate\", \"rung\": \"UNVERIFIED\",\n  \"reasoning\": \"...\", \"verdict\": \"...\",\n  \"future_state_condition\": \"<a not-yet-present condition>\",\n  \"enabling_assumption\":    \"<what must hold for it to arrive>\",\n  \"severity\": \"<minor|major|critical>\"? }\n```\n\n**`kind: \"situate\"`** — a best-in-class framing. Emit the SITUATE pipeline stages; the host composes +\nhonesty-caps the finding (`composeSituate`). **Tier-1 has no live researchPrime commission**, so\n`facts_verified` is `false` by construction and the host attaches the `needs_verification` handoff.\n```jsonc\n{ \"id\": \"s-1\", \"kind\": \"situate\", \"reasoning\": \"...\", \"verdict\": \"...\",\n  \"abstraction\":  { \"stage\": \"S0-abstract\", \"skeleton\": \"<domain-neutral pattern>\" },\n  \"commission\":   { \"skill\": \"researchPrime\", \"question\": \"...\", \"cross_model\": false,\n                    \"origin_family\": \"fable-5\", \"independent_origin\": false,\n                    \"researchprime_commission_id\": null },\n  \"structure_map\": { \"answer\": \"<answer-first conclusion>\",\n                     \"correspondences\": [\n                       { \"source_relation\": \"...\", \"target_relation\": \"...\" },\n                       { \"source_relation\": \"...\", \"target_relation\": \"...\" }  /* >= 2, RELATIONAL */\n                     ] },\n  \"outside_view_base_rate\": \"<the outside-view base rate>\" }\n```\n\nA finding of any other `kind` (or none) passes through untouched. A finding with `rung: \"REFUTED\"`\n**drops** (the only drop condition).\n\n### `elevations[]` — forward suggestions (NO tier, NO stamp)\n\nEmit the suggestion + the **named concrete defeater** (`what_would_refute_it`), never a tier or a\nstamp. In Tier-1 no independent refuter runs, so the host downgrades **every** elevation to\n`SPECULATIVE` and stamps it `\"no independent refutation ran\"` (`vetElevationRefutation` + `labelTier`).\n```jsonc\n{ \"id\": \"e-1\", \"value_if_true\": \"<low|medium|high>\", \"rung\": \"<...>\",\n  \"reasoning\": \"...\", \"verdict\": \"...\",\n  \"what_would_refute_it\": \"<a NAMED concrete defeater — never a confidence word>\",\n  \"severity\": \"<minor|major|critical>\"? }\n```\nA `rung: \"REFUTED\"` elevation **drops**.\n\n## What the host applies (deterministically, never the model)\n\n| Stage | Seam | Effect |\n|-------|------|--------|\n| diagnose | `seam/diagnose-core.stampDiagnoseCoreProvenance` | appends `gandalf_core: { protocol: \"PROTOCOL v2\" }` |\n| anticipate | `seam/anticipate.composeAnticipation` | `subject_cardinality: 1`; B3 + B9 enforced |\n| situate | `seam/situate.composeSituate` | rung cap (no self-CORROBORATED) + `needs_verification` handoff |\n| elevation | `seam/refute.vetElevationRefutation` → `seam/score-label.labelTier` | SPECULATIVE floor + stamp; single-family PROMISING ceiling |\n| drop | `seam/score-label.dropsFromOutput` | only `rung: \"REFUTED\"` drops |\n| synthesis | `seam/score-label.composeRiskLabels` | one `risk_labels` entry per present leg, envelope rung, PROMISING ceiling |\n| degradation | (host roll-up) | any per-item `degraded: true` ⇒ top-level `degraded: true` (B6) |\n\nThe result is validated by the shipped `test/harness.assertIncrement1Conformant` before it is written;\nif it would not pass, the host exits non-zero and writes nothing.\n\n## Scope note (Tier-1)\n\nThis host runs the **deterministic** seam pass on ONE model run. It does **not** dispatch the live\nindependent named-defeater refuters or the researchPrime SITUATE commission (those need the `agent()`\nseam the repo flags as the integration point the gate never runs). The **live-refuter PROMISING tier**\nis the sequenced follow-on — see `LESSONS.md` and `journal/`.\n","numLines":109,"startLine":1,"totalLines":109}}}
