om there to the Claude / Gemini / OpenClaw\nhosts) via `bin/sync-to-master.ps1`. `bin/check-map-drift.py` enforces that every\ndelivered target still matches its Foundry source.\n\nThe remaining consolidation is being completed wave-by-wave with the **Foreman**\norchestrator. The ground-truth gate for every wave is the pytest invariant suite\n`tests/test_foundry_invariants.py`, which only **grows** as waves land\n(anti-test-weakening).\n\n**Single-repo constraint.** Foreman commits within ONE git repo and gates on real\npytest. So Foreman does the Foundry-INTERNAL half (stage assets in, add governance\ndocs, extend the invariant suite). The cross-repo half — repointing external refs,\ndeleting sources in other repos, running the sync, publishing — is done MANUALLY as\nthe `FINALIZE` steps in the plan, because it spans git boundaries (Foreman's\nrepo-boundary guard would HALT on it).\n\nFull rationale: `C:\\dev\\Skill-Foundry-Foreman-Plan-20260603.md`.\nNarrative build history: `C:\\dev\\Skill-Foundry-Execution-Log.md`.\n","numLines":23,"startLine":1,"totalLines":23}}}
