{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_011US5YwjKUeJdx9ZUgeKQ8z","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# Gandalf v1 — LESSONS (anti-drift ledger)\n2\t\n3\t> Wave-7 scaffolding (the committed Gandalf v1 SHIP milestone). The running ledger of what the build\n4\t> learned and — load-bearing — the **anti-drift sleep gate** every Gandalf cycle passes through\n5\t> before it is allowed to conclude. The North Star is `NORTH-STAR.md` (LOCKED); this file records how\n6\t> the implementation is kept from drifting away from it.\n7\t\n8\t## The anti-drift sleep gate (the rule that keeps Gandalf on its North Star)\n9\t\n10\t**Canary set = the test suite.** The deterministic done-floor IS `node --test test/*.test.mjs`. There\n11\tis no second, hidden gate.\n12\t\n13\t**The sleep gate:** before any Gandalf cycle is considered DONE — before the skill \"sleeps\" / ships /\n14\thands back — the FULL canary set MUST be GREEN. A RED canary set BLOCKS the cycle from sleeping: a\n15\tfailing canary is a drift signal (the implementation has moved away from the LOCKED North Star), and\n16\tthe cycle may not conclude until it is GREEN again or the drift is escalated to a human re-lock.\n17\t\n18\tThe canary set the sleep gate runs (the Increment-1 deterministic done-floor):\n19\t\n20\t- **B1** zero ideation (ideation is Jumper's, not Gandalf's) · **B3** premortem ≠ Crucible's\n21\t  Oranges-engine (cardinality-1, no regret/counterfactual fields) · **B5** diagnose exclusive to the\n22\t  vetted core · **B6** no silent degradation · **B8** honest synthesis (every leg labelled, rung ≤\n23\t  envelope) · **B9** anticipate = not-yet-present future-state + enabling assumption · **B-honesty**\n24\t  named-defeater + refutation_provenance (or stamped SPECULATIVE) · **B-ceiling** single-family ⇒ max\n25\t  tier PROMISING.\n26\t- Each canary has a DISCRIMINATING NEGATIVE (a planted violation that MUST fail) — that is how the\n27\t  canary proves it tests a real invariant, not a tautology.\n28\t- The umbrella `assertIncrement1Conformant` runs the whole set over one output (the integration).\n29\t\n30\t**PRINCIPLE-D (what the sleep gate must NEVER become):** the LLM / cross-family judge and the\n31\televation oracle are **ADVISORY** — recorded as artifacts a human reads, NEVER part of the sleep\n32\tgate. The PRINCIPLE-D meta-isolation test proves this: with the judge endpoint made UNREACHABLE the\n33\tgate still exits 0, and the gate's static import closure provably excludes `seam/oracle.mjs`. If a\n34\tchange ever routes oracle/judge output into the gate, that test fails — the drift is caught.\n35\t\n36\t**WITHOUT-ledger honesty (B2′/B7′):** the anti-laundering content-binding canaries are\n37\tBLOCKED-this-cycle and NON-GATING (no Phase-0 ledger yet). The honor-system checklist\n38\t(`seam/anti-laundering.mjs`) surfaces that gap rather than hiding it; a forged commission-id rides\n39\tfree through the gate until the ledger lands (Increment 2). The sleep gate does not pretend\n40\totherwise.\n41\t\n42\t## Lessons\n43\t\n44\t- _(2026-06-22, runtime host — journal/0002)_ **The missing seam-pass wiring is now BUILT (Tier-1).**\n45\t  The journal/0001 follow-up — \"build a thin Gandalf runtime entry (model raw output → seam stamping →\n46\t  conformant output)\" — shipped as `runtime/seam-pass.applySeamPass` (the pure composer) +\n47\t  `runtime/gandalf-run.mjs` (the real CLI) + `runtime/RAW-DRAFT-CONTRACT.md` (the model now emits ONLY\n48\t  the raw draft and does NOT self-assign tiers/stamps — the host applies them). The host REUSES the\n49\t  shipped seams and reimplements NO grading logic; a malformed draft fails HONESTLY (`SeamPassInputError`\n50\t  → non-zero exit, no forged output). This directly closes the three over-claim failure modes from the\n51\t  first real run: the tiers + the \"no independent refutation ran\" stamp are now applied deterministically\n52\t  by `vetElevationRefutation` + `labelTier`, so the output is canary-conformant by construction.\n53\t  **SCOPE = Tier-1 deterministic:** ONE model run, NO live independent named-defeater refuters and NO\n54\t  researchPrime SITUATE commission (those need the `agent()` seam the gate never runs), so every elevation\n55\t  honestly lands at SPECULATIVE + the stamp and `risk_labels` cap at the single-family PROMISING ceiling.\n56\t  **The live-refuter PROMISING tier is the SEQUENCED FOLLOW-ON** — it needs the `agent()` seam, consistent\n57\t  with the Gandalf program's own dependency sequencing, and is NOT in this effort. Lesson reinforced: a\n58\t  skill plan must build the runtime that COMPOSES the model with its seams, not just the seams + canaries.\n59\t- _(2026-06-21, Wave 7)_ The integration wave's value was negative-space: proving the eight canaries\n60\t  hold TOGETHER on one real v1 output, and proving — structurally, via the import closure — that the\n61\t  advisory layer cannot leak into the gate. Asserting isolation is cheap; proving it is the point.\n62\t- _(2026-06-21, first real run — journal/0001)_ **The honesty stamps are the SEAM's job, not the\n63\t  model's — and the v1 runtime wiring is missing.** Dogfooding v1 on a webhook-idempotency note (3 passes)\n64\t  showed the model produces excellent DIAGNOSE/SITUATE/ANTICIPATE content but, run as pure SKILL.md prose\n65\t  with no seam pass, keeps hand-approximating tier stamps and failing B-honesty three different ways\n66\t  (named-defeater not a structured field → a below-threshold elevation stamped above SPECULATIVE → a\n67\t  SPECULATIVE elevation missing the literal \"no independent refutation ran\" stamp). Root cause: the honest\n68\t  tiers + stamps are meant to be APPLIED DETERMINISTICALLY by `seam/score-label.labelTier` +\n69\t  `seam/refute.{firesRefuter,composeRefutationProvenance,NO_INDEPENDENT_REFUTATION_STAMP}`, but the build\n70\t  shipped seams + canaries + SKILL.md with **no thin runtime entry** chaining model-content → seam-stamping →\n71\t  `assertIncrement1Conformant`. The canaries did their job (each caught a real over-claim); the fix is the\n72\t  missing seam-pass wiring, NOT more SKILL.md prose. SKILL.md §RUNTIME now documents the intended chain; the\n73\t  runtime entry is an open build follow-up. Same class as the SKILL.md-authoring gap → a skill plan must build\n74\t  the runtime that composes the model with its seams, not just the seams + canaries (PROGRAM-SEQUENCE lesson).\n75\t- _(seed)_ Append one bullet per cycle: what drifted, which canary caught it (or should have), and\n76\t  whether the North Star or a constant had to be re-locked by a human.\n77\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"362da09a-6bbc-452b-8ae5-c2595173c969","uuid":"dc445af1-aa08-47de-bf2b-7e7cb9bd260c","timestamp":"2026-06-23T18:46:33.365Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"C:\\dev\\Skill Foundry\\skills\\gandalf\\LESSONS.md","content":"# Gandalf v1 — LESSONS (anti-drift ledger)\n\n> Wave-7 scaffolding (the committed Gandalf v1 SHIP milestone). The running ledger of what the build\n> learned and — load-bearing — the **anti-drift sleep gate** every Gandalf cycle passes through\n> before it is allowed to conclude. The North Star is `NORTH-STAR.md` (LOCKED); this file records how\n> the implementation is kept from drifting away from it.\n\n## The anti-drift sleep gate (the rule that keeps Gandalf on its North Star)\n\n**Canary set = the test suite.** The deterministic done-floor IS `node --test test/*.test.mjs`. There\nis no second, hidden gate.\n\n**The sleep gate:** before any Gandalf cycle is considered DONE — before the skill \"sleeps\" / ships /\nhands back — the FULL canary set MUST be GREEN. A RED canary set BLOCKS the cycle from sleeping: a\nfailing canary is a drift signal (the implementation has moved away from the LOCKED North Star), and\nthe cycle may not conclude until it is GREEN again or the drift is escalated to a human re-lock.\n\nThe canary set the sleep gate runs (the Increment-1 determi