{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01MdD7ZPv6FDRA6HWtDXcXfZ","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# 0001 — first real run: webhook-idempotency design note (3-pass dogfood, 2026-06-21)\n2\t\n3\t> The first real Gandalf advisory cycles (a self-test right after v1 ship + promote). Provenance:\n4\t> genuine-execution (fresh-context sub-agents loaded SKILL.md and ran the protocol; output validated against\n5\t> `test/harness.mjs`). cross_model:false (single-family).\n6\t\n7\t## Effort\n8\tReviewed a compact engineering design note: *\"dedupe webhooks with an in-process `Set<string>` of `event_id`;\n9\tthis gives exactly-once processing with O(1) checks and no external dependencies.\"* (A planted-issue fixture:\n10\tthe in-memory Set is non-durable + non-shared + unbounded; best-in-class = a durable shared idempotency key;\n11\tcoming problems = restart-replay + scale-out divergence.)\n12\t\n13\t## Legs run + output (across 3 passes)\n14\t- **DIAGNOSE** (strong every pass): caught not-durable (restart loses dedup → exactly-once false), not-shared\n15\t  (per-instance under horizontal scale), exactly-once category-error (at-least-once channel), unbounded growth,\n16\t  AND an unprompted sharp one — check-then-act is **not atomic** (race + crash window). Operator-wrong pass\n17\t  nailed it: *\"'no external dependencies' is the root defect, not a feature.\"* Plus a steelman (the narrow\n18\t  single-process kernel).\n19\t- **SITUATE** (degraded, honest): named the durable-idempotency-key / inbox-pattern frame, structure-mapped\n20\t  (≥2 relational correspondences), stamped `degraded:true` + `UNVERIFIED` + `needs_verification` (researchPrime\n21\t  not commissioned). No self-CORROBORATED. Correct.\n22\t- **ANTICIPATE** (materialized in pass 2–3): two `kind:\"anticipate\"` findings (restart-replay wall; scale-out\n23\t  divergence wall) each with a `future_state_condition` + `enabling_assumption`, cardinality 1.\n24\t- **Output**: committed schema `gandalf/advisor-output/1`; final tiers E1=PROMISING (high, refuter survived),\n25\t  E2=SPECULATIVE (medium, below firing threshold). Single-family ceiling held (no GROUNDED).\n26\t\n27\t## Sleep gate / canary result — the harness DID ITS JOB (the value of the test)\n28\tThe deterministic harness caught the model OVER-CLAIMING honesty stamps on every pass, refusing each unearned\n29\ttier — exactly the anti-illusion spine working:\n30\t1. Pass 1: elevation stamped PROMISING but its named defeater was in PROSE, not the structured\n31\t   `what_would_refute_it`/`refutation_provenance` fields → B-honesty FAIL → auto-downgrade.\n32\t2. Pass 2: a `value_if_true:medium` elevation (below the refuter-firing threshold) stamped PROMISING → B-honesty\n33\t   FAIL → must ship SPECULATIVE.\n34\t3. Pass 3: the SPECULATIVE elevation lacked the literal \"no independent refutation ran\" stamp field → B-honesty FAIL.\n35\t\n36\t## Lesson (load-bearing — see LESSONS.md)\n37\tAll three are the SAME root cause: **the honest tiers + stamps are meant to be APPLIED DETERMINISTICALLY by the\n38\tseams (`score-label.labelTier`, `refute.firesRefuter`/`composeRefutationProvenance`/`NO_INDEPENDENT_REFUTATION_STAMP`),\n39\tnot hand-produced by the model.** The v1 build shipped the seams + canaries + SKILL.md but NO thin runtime entry\n40\tchaining model-content → seam-stamping → `assertIncrement1Conformant`. Tested as pure model-prose, the model\n41\tkeeps drifting on exact stamps. CONTENT quality is excellent; the gap is the missing seam-pass wiring.\n42\t\n43\t## Follow-ups opened\n44\t- Build a thin Gandalf runtime entry (model raw output → seam stamping pass → conformant output) — the missing\n45\t  host. (SKILL.md §RUNTIME now documents the intended chain; the entry itself is unbuilt.)\n46\t- This is the same class as the SKILL.md-authoring gap → reinforces the PROGRAM-SEQUENCE lesson: a skill plan\n47\t  must build the runtime that composes the model with its seams, not just the seams + canaries.\n48\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"362da09a-6bbc-452b-8ae5-c2595173c969","uuid":"e51532d7-2873-4807-bb93-1b5eb6a7a0bc","timestamp":"2026-06-23T18:46:34.778Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"C:\\dev\\Skill Foundry\\skills\\gandalf\\journal\\0001-first-real-run-webhook-idempotency.md","content":"# 0001 — first real run: webhook-idempotency design note (3-pass dogfood, 2026-06-21)\n\n> The first real Gandalf advisory cycles (a self-test right after v1 ship + promote). Provenance:\n> genuine-execution (fresh-context sub-agents loaded SKILL.md and ran the protocol; output validated against\n> `test/harness.mjs`). cross_model:false (single-family).\n\n## Effort\nReviewed a compact engineering design note: *\"dedupe webhooks with an in-process `Set<string>` of `event_id`;\nthis gives exactly-once processing with O(1) checks and no external dependencies.\"* (A planted-issue fixture:\nthe in-memory Set is non-durable + non-shared + unbounded; best-in-class = a durable shared idempotency key;\ncoming problems = restart-replay + scale-out divergence.)\n\n## Legs run + output (across 3 passes)\n- **DIAGNOSE** (strong every pass): caught not-durable (restart loses dedup → exactly-once false), not-shared\n  (per-instance under horizontal scale), exactly-once category-error (at-least-once channel), unbounded growth,\n  AND an unprompted sharp one — check-then-act is **not atomic** (race + crash window). Operator-wrong pass\n  nailed it: *\"'no external dependencies' is the root defect, not a feature.\"* Plus a steelman (the narrow\n  single-process kernel).\n- **SITUATE** (degraded, honest): named the durable-idempotency-key / inbox-pattern frame, structure-mapped\n  (≥2 relational correspondences), stamped `degraded:true` + `UNVERIFIED` + `needs_verification` (researchPrime\n  not commissioned). No self-CORROBORATED. Correct.\n- **ANTICIPATE** (materialized in pass 2–3): two `kind:\"anticipate\"` findings (restart-replay wall; scale-out\n  divergence wall) each with a `future_state_condition` + `enabling_assumption`, cardinality 1.\n- **Output**: committed schema `gandalf/advisor-output/1`; final tiers E1=PROMISING (high, refuter survived),\n  E2=SPECULATIVE (medium, below firing threshold). Single-family ceiling held (no GROUNDED).\n\n## Sleep gate / canary result — the harness DID ITS JOB (the value of the test)\nThe deterministic harness caught the model OVER-CLAIMING honesty stamps on every pass, refusing each unearned\ntier — exactly the anti-illusion spine working:\n1. Pass 1: elevation stamped PROMISING but its named defeater was in PROSE, not the structured\n   `what_would_refute_it`/`refutation_provenance` fields → B-honesty FAIL → auto-downgrade.\n2. Pass 2: a `value_if_true:medium` elevation (below the refuter-firing threshold) stamped PROMISING → B-honesty\n   FAIL → must ship SPECULATIVE.\n3. Pass 3: the SPECULATIVE elevation lacked the literal \"no independent refutation ran\" stamp field → B-honesty FAIL.\n\n## Lesson (load-bearing — see LESSONS.md)\nAll three are the SAME root cause: **the honest tiers + stamps are meant to be APPLIED DETERMINISTICALLY by the\nseams (`score-label.labelTier`, `refute.firesRefuter`/`composeRefutationProvenance`/`NO_INDEPENDENT_REFUTATION_STAMP`),\nnot hand-produced by the model.** The v1 build shipped the seams + canaries + SKILL.md but NO thin runtime entry\nchaining model-content → seam-stamping → `assertIncrement1Conformant`. Tested as pure model-prose, the model\nkeeps drifting on exact stamps. CONTENT quality is excellent; the gap is the missing seam-pass wiring.\n\n## Follow-ups opened\n- Build a thin Gandalf runtime entry (model raw output → seam stamping pass → conformant output) — the missing\n  host. (SKILL.md §RUNTIME now documents the intended chain; the entry itself is unbuilt.)\n- This is the same class as the SKILL.md-authoring gap → reinforces the PROGRAM-SEQUENCE lesson: a skill plan\n  must build the runtime that composes 